register_gate "tests/test_force_rls_enumeration.py" "FORCE-RLS ENUMERATION GATE: PASS" "FORCE-RLS enumeration" "FORCE-RLS enumeration (every multi-tenant core.* table is FORCE-RLS-locked + carries a tenant_isolation policy; the four cross-tenant operational tables credential / installation_account / account_lifecycle_tombstone / account_plan_event / webhook_delivery / active_alert are intentionally walled by REVOKE ALL FROM PUBLIC instead -- the allowlist is integrity-checked; probe validity proven by a known-FORCE-locked table reading true and the known-allowlisted webhook_delivery reading false)" "FORCE-RLS enumeration: the runtime catalog audit (Round-2 perimeter follow-up). Reads pg_class.relforcerowsecurity for every regular core.* table; treats a table as multi-tenant iff it carries one of account_id / account_key / follower_account / grantor_account / created_by_account (the live schema's tenant-scope columns); asserts every non-allowlisted multi-tenant table reports relforcerowsecurity=true; asserts a paired tenant_isolation policy exists (FORCE without a policy denies every write). Catches the silent-regression class: a new core table that ships with account_id but without the matching FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY line, where the SECURITY DEFINER owner could land cross-tenant writes" 24
